import json
from pathlib import Path
b=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;s=json.loads((b/'summary.json').read_text());lines=['# PR #642: post-rebase full benchmark and review','', 'Date: 2026-11-07 (Asia/Shanghai). PR #642 is merged as af4b07b22adf9f08586f9dd08adb1d57a07cce51. Its complete source tree equals measured head e678e1ee9b2d921b0079d33c00be768186d886de (tree 04abe5b1a2cbf8890a1c007f4d77eddb0e535237). The before-merge baseline is 59fe3cc9ec0c9cf3c06c411c4ed1fb0b2460ff9c, including #641.', '', '## Findings and interpretation','', 'No definite new runtime correctness defect was found in the reviewed production changes. All 30 PolyBench cases completed on all three engines with identical full stdout/stderr hashes. All 16 combined lazy JIT unit tests were rerun and passed. This does not establish correctness on all hosts or workloads.', '', 'P2: the committed benchmark.py at docs/changes/2026-11-06-lazy-numeric-loop-firstcall/benchmark.py:67 hardcodes main_commit=193b8d2 even when --main selects another build. This mislabels experiments against 59fe3cc or later. Record explicit user-supplied revisions (or unknown), alongside executable hashes. This report uses an independent archived driver with actual frozen revisions and raw byte output hashes.', '', 'Coverage gap: the two selected numeric fixtures call a helper outside their qualifying loop, so they are not eligible for #641 private promotion. Turning private tiering on therefore does not directly exercise the guard that prevents a function already selected for initial Greedy from installing a private FastRA profiling gate. Add a pure FP positive with enough live values to spill, low thresholds and assertions against private probing.', '', 'The 3-round durbin +28% screen did not replicate: 21 new rounds favor the merged implementation in every paired round. The WAPM pi/qr2text/uuid negatives also did not replicate. Suggest/viu group medians can look 5–8% worse, but paired intervals cross 1; neither regression nor equivalence is established. Floyd screen +5.4% did not replicate in the independent mode cohort. All negative screens remain in raw samples.', '', 'Integer mode controls identify a new opportunity: serial lazy (configured Greedy) is much faster than default lazy MT for Floyd/Nussinov. This changes threading AND allocator mode, so it is an ablation/hypothesis, not proof that a new MT policy is profitable. A separate production candidate and startup checks are needed before a new optimization PR.', '', '## Protocol','', 'Fresh processes, warm file-page cache, one excluded warmup per case/engine (round -1), randomized within-round order, CPU 0 including workers. DTVM is Release GCC 14.2 / LLVM15, multipass lazy MT, private tiering default OFF. Wasmtime 45 cache disabled (-C cache=n). Main and merged binaries use identical production build options; SPEC/ASAN/EVM/profiling/logging/perf OFF, WASI and checked arithmetic ON. Timing runs had no concurrent builds/tests/profiles. Exact options, inputs and commands are in environment.json and each manifest.', '', 'Wall time includes spawn, startup, compilation, execution, captured output and teardown, including full PolyBench matrix printing. Hashing/compression are outside the timed boundary. This is not isolated kernel timing. Wasmtime45 is the existing repository artifact, not independently rebuilt here. One Linux x86-64 host/affinity setup is not a multi-host claim.', '', 'An environment restart interrupted the first integer-mode warmup, before any timed round. integer-modes-r3 is explicitly incomplete and excluded; its raw sample remains. integer-modes-resumed-r3 starts afresh with a new seed and recorded resumed environment. Completed earlier cohorts are retained separately, never pooled.', '', 'Group medians and within-round paired median ratios are different statistics. Intervals below use 10,000 percentile bootstrap resamples of within-round ratios, fixed seed 2026110742, pointwise 95% without multiple-comparison correction. Three-round screens are exploratory; their intervals should not be read as precise significance claims.', '', 'Frozen main SHA256: ed77ecc2816738e2a7a8c97de3a8ea991da32a252624b43bb1fdb815e1f2ecfd. Merged-implementation SHA256: 7e0e041f0faaa461feb8f651df77886882167a68f73e50a43251354382965002. All engine hashes are in manifests.', '']
for cohort,title in [('matrix-confirm-r9','Matrix confirmation: 9 rounds'),('polybench-r3','All 30 PolyBench: 3-round screen'),('wapm-r7','All 20 WAPM: 7-round screen'),('startup-confirm-r21','Startup and negative-screen confirmation: 21 rounds'),('integer-modes-resumed-r3','Integer mode control: 3 rounds after restart')]:
 lines+=['## '+title,'', 'Milliseconds; change is ratio of group medians, not paired median ratio.','', '| Case | Before #642 | Merged lazy MT | WT45 | Change vs baseline |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for c,d in s[cohort].items():
  m=d['medians_ms']
  if not d['valid_exit'] or not m:lines.append(f'| {c} | exit 1 | exit 1 | exit 1 | excluded |');continue
  lines.append(f"| {c} | {m['main']:.3f} | {m['candidate']:.3f} | {m['wt45']:.3f} | {100*(m['candidate']/m['main']-1):+.1f}% |")
 if cohort in ['matrix-confirm-r9','startup-confirm-r21']:
  lines+=['','| Case | Paired merged/baseline | 95% interval | Paired merged/WT45 | 95% interval |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
  for c,d in s[cohort].items():
   p=d['paired_ratios']['candidate/main'];q=d['paired_ratios']['candidate/wt45'];x,y=p['pointwise_bootstrap95'];u,v=q['pointwise_bootstrap95'];lines.append(f"| {c} | {p['paired_median']:.4f} | [{x:.4f}, {y:.4f}] | {q['paired_median']:.4f} | [{u:.4f}, {v:.4f}] |")
 if cohort=='integer-modes-resumed-r3':
  lines+=['','| Case | Merged lazy MT | Same binary serial Greedy | WT45 |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
  for c,d in s[cohort].items():
   m=d['medians_ms'];lines.append(f"| {c} | {m['candidate']:.3f} | {m['candidate-serial']:.3f} | {m['wt45']:.3f} |")
 lines+=['']
lines+=['## Output and validation limits','','WAPM sam returns 1 on all three engines under the catalog invocation; it is recorded once per engine and excluded from performance medians. Its stdout contains non-UTF8 bytes; the runner captures bytes without decoding loss. Fortune and UUID text varies naturally; other successful WAPM full outputs are identical across engines/rounds. IRB actually computes 3+4 => 7 with matching prompts/results. Amirali prints its contact text (including NUL padding). No input was silently replaced to manufacture a speedup.','','Executable artifacts and compressed/deduplicated full outputs remain in the execution workspace. The public archive retains every timing/exit/hash sample, commands, environment, output byte counts/previews and analysis scripts, without uploading repeated huge matrices. Empty/review format and older WAST/MIR logs from prior work are not represented as new reruns. This task reran 16 lazy tests and rebuilt both production revisions.','']
(b/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
